<PageLayout title="Download Grok Chats" description="Back up your Grok conversations from xAI with TotalRecalls." breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Guides", href: "/guides/" }, { label: "Grok" }]}>
  <h1>Downloading Grok Conversations</h1>
  <p>TotalRecalls reads your Grok (grok.com) session from its own sign-in window and downloads every conversation to local Markdown and JSON.</p>
  
  <h2>Steps</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Launch TotalRecalls and select <strong>Grok</strong> as the provider.</li>
    <li>Click <strong>Log in to Grok</strong>. A sign-in window opens inside the app &mdash; sign in there. Your credentials stay on your machine.</li>
    <li>Pick a destination folder under <strong>Where to save</strong>. Every conversation is written as both Markdown and JSON; there is no format choice to make.</li>
    <li>Click <strong>Download my conversations</strong>. Use <strong>Download latest only</strong> for a quick refresh.</li>
    <li>When it finishes, click <strong>Open folder</strong> to see your files.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Notes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Grok does offer an account-level export under <strong>Settings &rarr; Data Controls</strong>, but it produces one whole-account archive. TotalRecalls writes one readable Markdown + JSON pair per conversation instead.</li>
    <li>X posts referenced in chats are preserved as quoted links in the Markdown download.</li>
  </ul>
</PageLayout>
